.PP
A typed read passes a tag that the path does not read (section 7), so
\f[CR]at_path<\(dq$\(dq, int>\f[R] reads 5 from \f[CR]1(5)\f[R] and
\f[CR]at_path<\(dq$\(dq, std::string_view>\f[R] reads the text of
\f[CR]32(\(dqx\(dq)\f[R].
The free form over bytes also takes \f[CR]std::string\f[R] and
\f[CR]std::vector<std::byte>\f[R], and copies the value (section 1).
Any other T does not compile, for example \f[CR]float\f[R] or a view
without an owner.
For any other result, read the node of \f[CR]lazy.at_path<Path>()\f[R].
