.SS 11. What the form over bytes checks
A path reads the heads from the start of the item to the target, and the
heads and strings that it skips on the way.
Each data item has at least one byte, so an array or a map that claims
more items than the bytes left gives \f[CR]too_little_data\f[R] before
any element is read.
A path does not read the bytes after the target.
So these faults are not found:
.PP
